.TH LIBMPQ__PATCH_PAYLOAD_SIZE 3 2026-10-06 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__patch_payload_size \- return the decoded PTCH payload size.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.sp
.BI "int32_t libmpq__patch_payload_size("
.BI "        mpq_archive_s *" "archive,"
.BI "        uint32_t " "file_number,"
.BI "        libmpq__off_t *" "size"
.BI ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
For a member flagged \fBLIBMPQ_FILE_FLAG_PATCH_FILE\fP, return the size of
its decoded PTCH body after the plaintext patch-info prefix. This differs
from \fBlibmpq__file_size_unpacked\fP(3), which reports the patched target
size stored in the MPQ block table. No patch is applied.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns zero on success and stores the size in \fIsize\fP. On failure,
\fIsize\fP is zero and a negative libmpq error is returned.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B LIBMPQ_ERROR_EXIST
The archive, output pointer, file number, or patch-file flag is absent.
.TP
.B LIBMPQ_ERROR_FORMAT
The patch-info prefix is malformed or truncated.
.PP
Source I/O errors may also propagate.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmpq__patch_payload_read (3),
.BR libmpq__file_flags (3),
.BR libmpq__file_size_unpacked (3)
